      "content": "I apologize for the confusion caused by my previous response. Let's address your concerns with the appropriate level of seriousness and focus on the legal aspects of the \"unaided memory\" provision.\n\nThe \"unaided memory\" provision in the NDA clause is a critical point of concern when it comes to the protection of intellectual property (IP). In legal terms, the distinction between \"general professional expertise\" and \"proprietary structural logic\" is often nuanced and can be highly fact-specific. Courts typically look at several factors to determine whether the knowledge retained in one's memory is proprietary or general.\n\nFirstly, the specificity and uniqueness of the information in question are paramount. Proprietary structural logic would be characterized by its distinctiveness and the degree to which it is not commonly known or used in the industry. Courts will examine whether the information is easily replicable by others without access to the proprietary logic.\n\nSecondly, the extent of the individual's exposure to the proprietary information is considered. If the individual has had extensive and exclusive access to the confidential information, this could weigh in favor of the information being proprietary.\n\nThirdly, the manner in which the individual has used the information is scrutinized. If the individual has applied the proprietary logic in a way that is demonstrably different from general",
